<author id="708738">LanX</author>
<doctext field_name="doctext"> 
&gt; plus I imagine certain set operations would be problematic due to floating-point inaccuracies.&lt;P&gt;

I doubt this, rounding errors happen only after arithmetic operations&lt;P&gt;

as long as two floats are different, comparisons will show a strict order:&lt;P&gt;


&lt;c&gt;
  DB&lt;95&gt; $one = 1-1e-16

  DB&lt;96&gt; printf '%.17f', $one
0.99999999999999989
  DB&lt;97&gt; p 1 &gt; $one
1
  DB&lt;98&gt; $one = 1-1e-16

  DB&lt;99&gt; p $one
1
  DB&lt;100&gt;
&lt;/c&gt;&lt;P&gt;

FWIW &lt;C&gt;0.1e-1&lt;/C&gt; and &lt;C&gt;1e-2&lt;/C&gt; are the same float in my books.&lt;P&gt;

